.TH IDIOT-TEST 1 "2026-07-21" "zdots" "zdots manual"
.SH NAME
idiot-test \- idiot\-test — an advisory gate for destructive commands.
.SH SYNOPSIS
See OPTIONS below (generated from \fBidiot-test --help\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
idiot-test — an advisory gate for destructive commands.

Applies the Idiot Test ("would an idiot do this?") to a proposed command and
screens it for catastrophic filesystem operations — the class that wiped this
machine on 2026-05-25 (an agent ran `rm -rf ~/`). See: agent-guide, the
"Filesystem Doctrine" section.

This is a BACKSTOP, not a substitute for thinking. It is heuristic: it can miss
things and it can be bypassed. A "pass" is not permission to skip resolving and
reading your targets. The doctrine ("think first") stays primary.

Usage:
  idiot-test <command...>     screen argv         (exit 0 ok · 1 warn · 2 block)
  echo "<cmd>" | idiot-test   screen stdin
  idiot-test --hook           Claude Code PreToolUse hook: read the tool JSON on
                              stdin, screen Bash commands, exit 2 to BLOCK on a
                              catastrophic pattern, 0 otherwise (never blocks
                              non-destructive commands).
  idiot-test -h | --help
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
agent-guide(1), zdots-doctor(1)
